00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:33.040
So let's start with the first tip.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.160
And indeed, let me share a story.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.470
This is from an instance
that really happened

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:39.690
during my consulting professional life.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:42.330
I was on a project and
we were having a workshop

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.260
with a client.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.880
I was the responsible associate

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:46.910
who was supposed to cover this workshop.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.420
So I sat together with a
client who was organizing it

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:50.620
from the client's side.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.420
I discussed it with him a little bit.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:54.940
I helped him draft some of the
materials for the workshop.

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.040
But then it looked all good.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.500
The workshop was prepared

00:02:57.500 --> 00:02:58.640
and then was happening.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.190
On the workshop day the client
was leading the workshop

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:03.510
and I was pretty much just sitting there.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:05.610
I was still a young associate.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:06.890
He was presenting everything

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:09.500
and I tried it to make a
couple of remarks and comments

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:10.333
which I felt like were probably smart

00:03:10.333 --> 00:03:12.420
and we're adding value.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.780
But the truth also is
that in this long workshop

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:17.110
I didn't really add much
to the conversation.

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.180
And this is then indeed
also point of feedback

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:21.550
that I got from the project
lead after the workshop.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:22.637
And she was telling me,

00:03:22.637 --> 00:03:24.597
"Well, Heinrich, you
were a bit too passive.

00:03:24.597 --> 00:03:26.847
"You were not active
enough as an associate.

00:03:26.847 --> 00:03:27.797
"It should have been your role

00:03:27.797 --> 00:03:29.750
"to shape the whole workshop a bit more."

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:32.030
So what I realized from
this episode is that

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:33.960
what I didn't do, what I should have done

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.280
is to clarify my role before the meeting.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.120
And this is indeed the first tip

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.290
that I want to share with you.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:42.840
Make sure that you clarify your role.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.990
And this is true, both
for external meetings

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.730
but also for internal meetings.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:49.100
Often our setting was in
these internal meetings.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.140
There are some partners,

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.560
some senior partners, the project lead,

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:55.440
and then you're sitting
there as a young associate,

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.810
as a young consultant.

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:58.030
And then often you're lost.

00:03:58.030 --> 00:03:59.710
I mean, what are you supposed to add

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:00.940
to the conversation, right?

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.590
And indeed then especially
when also clients are present,

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:05.710
then it's often the task
of the project lead,

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:09.030
or maybe even the partner
to moderate the discussion.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.580
And often in these situations

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:12.450
you are as the junior guy,

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:15.500
also not the deepest subject matter expert

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.310
at the topic that is being discussed.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:20.620
So on the content level,
you will also often struggle

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:23.000
to really participate and to add value,

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.290
especially in these situations

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:26.460
where all of these other
senior guys are present.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:29.910
So my advice is that before
these meetings are taking place,

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.890
talk to the responsible person.

00:04:31.890 --> 00:04:33.930
So this might be your client counterpart,

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:35.160
or maybe a project lead.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.920
If now you're walking
into an internal meeting

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:38.690
with all your partners, really ask them,

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:39.660
how can you add value?

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.100
What should your role be?

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:42.440
And maybe make some suggestions.

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:43.640
What do you believe you could do.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:44.610
And just some examples.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:45.500
So what could you do?

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.720
So for instance, if you
present a larger document

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.270
maybe you would agree on a
certain section in the document

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:52.200
that you will present, that you will lead.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.440
Maybe there will be a
certain flip chart session

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:55.590
during the workshop

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:57.420
and then you can lead this little session,

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:00.220
collect all the questions,
steer the whole discussion.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.810
Maybe you will be the one
who writes all the notes

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:05.020
and then in the end writes
the meeting minutes.

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:06.220
So all of these are little things

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:08.240
that can increase your participation.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:11.580
Your activeness will also
increase your visibility.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.360
And if you are a regular
watcher of my channel,

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.600
you know how important in my opinion

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.070
visibility is for your career success.

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:19.330
And I specially made one video

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:20.830
about this topic of visibility.

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:22.630
I will link it somewhere above here.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:24.420
It is also one of my older videos

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.500
but I believe the message in there

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:28.510
are still very, very valid.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:31.730
Now for tip number two, let
me share an additional story.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.130
And this is something that happened to me

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:34.600
when I was a project lead

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.660
and probably a similar
thing's also happened to me

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.020
with vigorous roles when
I was a more junior guy

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:39.853
on the team.

00:05:39.853 --> 00:05:41.460
But at that instance,
I was a project lead.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.140
I was sitting in a meeting
with one of my associates

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:46.330
and he also was a more junior associate.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:48.780
He was only with the firm
for a couple of months.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:49.880
And we were sitting at a meeting

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.790
which was part of his module, right?

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:53.670
So pretty much the meeting was in the end

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.660
his responsibility in the sense that

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.660
he was responsible to cover
the topics that were discussed.

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:00.680
So then during the meeting,
I as a project lead

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.570
tried to moderate the whole discussion

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:04.800
to steer the conversation
in the right direction.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.550
But then there were occasional moments

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:08.800
where people were asking us about data,

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:10.450
about files that the sent us,

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:13.170
what certain numbers were,
how this all added up.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:16.040
And my associate was just
sitting there pretty quiet,

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:16.980
pretty shy.

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.550
Didn't really say anything.

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:20.410
So then I ended up opening my laptop,

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:22.460
pulling out some files
and pretty much sharing

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.410
some pieces of information
that I wanted to share

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:25.250
back with the client.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:26.560
And of course, to some extent here

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:27.900
my expectation would have been,

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.210
this is something that
the associate would do.

00:06:30.210 --> 00:06:31.510
That as the module owner,

00:06:31.510 --> 00:06:33.440
he would have all these files at hand

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:36.050
and would be able to share all
these numbers in the meeting.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:37.840
And this now leads me to tip number two.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:38.673
And this is that,

00:06:38.673 --> 00:06:40.880
especially as the junior guy in the room.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.380
Be the numbers guy.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:44.030
So especially if this is a meeting

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:46.470
that is about one of the
topics that you are covering.

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:49.230
In these instances it actually
would even be expected

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:51.790
that of course, you know
all your data much better

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:53.640
and much more in detail
than the project lead.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:56.050
Also needs to manage
other parts of the project

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:57.630
parallel to this specific part.

00:06:57.630 --> 00:06:59.830
Of course you will have
all your files at hand.

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:02.300
Of course you will know
the most important numbers

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:04.620
concerning this work
probably even in your head.

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:06.460
You will not even need
a file for that, right?

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:09.380
So of course if questions
are asked about these topics,

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:10.420
this is your moment.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:12.660
This is your role where you can jump in

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:15.360
and then share all this
information that you have at hand.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.830
So being the numbers guy,
it's a straightforward

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:20.280
and actually pretty easy
little thing that you can do

00:07:20.280 --> 00:07:22.230
as the junior guy to add some value

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:23.850
by providing the relevant data.

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:25.400
And I'd say, even if it's a question

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:26.900
which is not directly belonging

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:28.830
to your area of responsibility,

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.760
don't let your project
lead or your partner,

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:33.040
on a corporate context,
your boss or whatever,

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:33.940
look this stuff up.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:35.750
If you have it, then
take this as your role.

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:37.640
You are the one who can
quickly look this up.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:39.600
Ideally already come into the meeting

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.130
with maybe your laptop opened

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.610
with the most important
files or spreadsheets

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:44.830
which will likely to be the focus

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.400
of the discussion already opened.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.920
So that if such a question comes up,

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:50.370
you do not need to
first look for this file

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:52.310
where you have saved
it, open it and so on,

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:53.537
but you directly have it in front of you.

00:07:53.537 --> 00:07:55.460
You can directly tell them the numbers.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:58.100
These are these little great
moments where you can shine.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:07:59.370
Where you can add value.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:01.200
And these are things
that will be perceived

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:03.000
by your team and also by the clients.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.090
So tip number three.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:05.320
And now again, a little story

00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:07.040
from the perception of a project lead.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:10.270
So often, which join meetings
that your associates scheduled

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:13.450
that are with clients that
are covered by your associates

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.510
just because of the
topic is a bit sensitive

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.810
or maybe the client has
quite a personality.

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:20.090
That maybe the associate
asked you to also jump in,

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:22.410
to sit in there to try to
help him to steer the meeting

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:23.490
into the right direction.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.692
So, one thing that I
observed occasionally was,

00:08:25.692 --> 00:08:27.131
(mumbles) I was sitting in these meetings,

00:08:27.131 --> 00:08:30.670
I was trying to help and I
thought it was a great meeting.

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:32.870
And then the meeting was
over, all the clients left

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:34.177
and I was sitting there with the associate

00:08:34.177 --> 00:08:35.817
and then I asked him or her,

00:08:35.817 --> 00:08:36.650
"Hey, what do you think?

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:37.540
"How did the meeting go?"

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:38.637
And then the associate says,

00:08:38.637 --> 00:08:39.837
"Well, yes. It went well.

00:08:39.837 --> 00:08:41.367
"But we didn't ask the question.

00:08:41.367 --> 00:08:43.147
"We didn't got this piece of information

00:08:43.147 --> 00:08:44.170
"that we really needed."

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:45.400
And then this often confuse me.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.147
And then I asked the person,

00:08:47.147 --> 00:08:47.980
"Well, okay.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:49.817
"But if you know that this was important,

00:08:49.817 --> 00:08:52.147
"if you know that we needed
to ask this question as well,

00:08:52.147 --> 00:08:53.297
"then why didn't you ask?"

00:08:53.297 --> 00:08:55.720
And this was something that
I occasionally observed

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.230
with more junior consultants

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:59.450
that as soon as somebody
more senior than them

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:01.660
sits in the meeting, sits in the room.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.060
Sometimes they feel like, okay,

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.500
now the meeting isn't my
responsibility anymore.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:06.550
Or maybe they are too shy

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:08.603
and believe that well, if
this would be really important

00:09:08.603 --> 00:09:10.700
then probably my project
lead or my partner

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:11.533
would think of that.

00:09:11.533 --> 00:09:13.650
But of course often it's
the other way round, right?

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:16.040
Often the partner is the furthest away

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:17.880
from what is actually
going on in the project.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:19.520
And the project lead will as well

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:22.200
be already much further away
than you as an associate.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.840
So take this as your
responsibility as well.

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:26.200
And this is my third tip.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:28.510
So make sure that all the key results,

00:09:28.510 --> 00:09:31.770
that all the next steps are
really clear and defined.

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:33.800
And if you feel like for whatever reason

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.830
that something important
is just not raised

00:09:35.830 --> 00:09:37.560
by the more senior people in the room,

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:39.350
but you know that it is important,

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:40.183
then raise it.

00:09:40.183 --> 00:09:41.300
Then ask the question.

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:42.150
Then address it.

00:09:42.150 --> 00:09:44.900
Do not believe that that is
not your role to ask this

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:47.520
or that you're too intimidated
to address this point

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.010
that you know is so important.

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:50.570
Of course be aware of politics.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:51.990
Maybe it's a very sensitive thing.

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:53.850
Maybe there was a reason
that the project lead

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:55.900
or whoever was sitting in there
with you, didn't raise it.

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:57.420
So of course try to be sensitive

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.780
for these types of things as well.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.070
But in general, I believe
that it really rarely hurts

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:03.950
if you as the junior guy really
pushed for tangible results

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:05.460
and next steps that I
agreed in the meeting.

00:10:05.460 --> 00:10:07.500
So I hope that you find
these three tips helpful.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:09.350
So first clarify your role.

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.090
Second, be the number guy.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.910
And third, push for clear
next steps and results.

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:14.743
If you do this

00:10:14.743 --> 00:10:17.080
I trust you will add lots
of value to the meeting.

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:18.740
